{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463268",
      "title": "Using v-show Instead Of v-if",
      "lectureOrder": 45,
      "videoOrder": 40,
      "sourceHash": "3e4a5ba982358afbad7fdc4178044a09acf8b0dc5ed5eae2e79b2274426783b8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.76,
          "en": "Now there is an alternative to v-if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.76,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "There is nothing wrong with v-if,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.02,
          "end": 9.443,
          "en": "but there also is v-show,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 15.32,
          "en": "v-show does not work together with v-else or v-else-if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.46,
          "end": 17.96,
          "en": "It only works stand-alone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.96,
          "end": 20.87,
          "en": "and therefore if you have multiple alternatives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.87,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "you really need to use multiple v-shows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 25.45,
          "en": "That's one difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.45,
          "end": 27.6,
          "en": "But what does v-show do then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.6,
          "end": 29.81,
          "en": "It seems to be more complicated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.81,
          "end": 32.52,
          "en": "It doesn't have to simplifications with v-else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 33.64,
          "en": "and v-else-if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.64,
          "end": 36.26,
          "en": "So, why would we use v-show?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.26,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "There's one important difference regarding its behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 43.42,
          "en": "If I reload, we don't see a huge difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.42,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "It works in the same way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 49,
          "en": "but let me reload again and let's inspect this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49,
          "end": 50.95,
          "en": "And then you'll notice a difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.95,
          "end": 52.79,
          "en": "The paragraph is there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.79,
          "end": 54.603,
          "en": "but so is the unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.48,
          "end": 59.47,
          "en": "And the only difference is that the unordered list is hidden",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.47,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "because its display style is set to none",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 64.67,
          "en": "and that's the difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.67,
          "end": 69.67,
          "en": "V-if really removes and adds elements from and to the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.43,
          "end": 75.35,
          "en": "So it really impacts which elements are part of the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.35,
          "end": 76.93,
          "en": "v-show on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.93,
          "end": 80.57300000000001,
          "en": "just hides and show items with CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.42,
          "end": 83.89,
          "en": "Now, which approach is better?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.89,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "Showing and hiding with CSS means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "that you don't have to add and remove elements all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 92.13,
          "en": "which can cost performance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.13,
          "end": 95.92,
          "en": "adding and removing elements can cost performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.92,
          "end": 97.1,
          "en": "On the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.1,
          "end": 99.83,
          "en": "it also means that you have a bunch of elements in your DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.83,
          "end": 101.64,
          "en": "which you don't really need at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.64,
          "end": 103.78999999999999,
          "en": "which also is not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.78999999999999,
          "end": 105.92,
          "en": "Therefore, as a rule of thumb,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.92,
          "end": 110.92,
          "en": "you should typically use v-if and only fall back to v-show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.21000000000001,
          "end": 112.62,
          "en": "if you have an element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 115.97999999999999,
          "en": "which visibility status changes a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.97999999999999,
          "end": 118.75,
          "en": "So, if you have like a button that toggles an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.75,
          "end": 120.83,
          "en": "and it's switching between visibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.83,
          "end": 122.53,
          "en": "and being hidden all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.53,
          "end": 125.3,
          "en": "that is when you might want to consider v-show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.3,
          "end": 128.12,
          "en": "in other cases use v-if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.12,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "And that's why I'm going to switch back to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 133.42,
          "en": "But I wanna show you, v-show as an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.42,
          "end": 136.87,
          "en": "because of course it is important to know that as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.87,
          "end": 139.89,
          "en": "for situations where you have content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.89,
          "end": 143.28300000000002,
          "en": "that switches a lot between being visible and being hidden.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
